== bot pvp-check

> loot-survivor-bot@1.0.0 bot
> node --import tsx src/cli.ts pvp-check

Loot Survivor bot

Usage: npm run bot -- <command> [options]

  play         Play games (practice or mainnet) and write dashboard data
  sim          Simulate one game locally and print the decision log
  bench        Benchmark the current policy over many simulated games
  tune         Optimize policy parameters with CMA-ES on simulated games (multi-core)
  dataset      Export simulated states for the GPU trainer (trainer/)
  discover     Fetch live contract ABIs, presets and API endpoints; write data/discovery
  leaderboard  Fetch the mainnet leaderboard and live players; write site/data
  learn        Learn from top players: ingest their games and update insights
  authorize    One-time Cartridge Controller session authorization for mainnet play
  site         Rebuild site/data summaries from the bot data directory
  local        Local GPU learning loop: self-play dataset -> value net (PyTorch) -> A/B -> tune
  leaders      Download the full event history of the top leaderboard games for analysis
  v2-inspect   Validate the V2 commit-reveal read path on live mainnet games (no account needed)
  validate     A/B a candidate policy on the official site engine (practice) and adopt it only if better
  dungeon-settings Read dungeon game settings (e.g. Ronke Casino #7) from the V2 game core
  site-config  Write site/bot-config.json (session policies and RPC for approving the bot on the website)
  ronke        Ronke Casino daily free games: status for the bot account, --claim to claim today's games
  reach        Probability of reaching deep levels (multilevel splitting) for one or more policies (--policy a.json,b.json)
  contract     Inspect live mainnet contracts: ABI and view calls (--address 0x.. --call name:arg,arg)
  pvp          PvP Dungeons with the invited Game Account: submit/claim earlier tables, play today's table (--live, --max-games runs, --minutes)
  http-get     GET public JSON endpoints and print status and body (--address url, repeatable)
  rpc-probe    Raw answers of the RPC endpoints (chainId, specVersion, Cartridge paymaster) to see which still speak JSON-RPC
  v2-dryrun    Dry-run the bot's next move in a game and print why the core would reject it (--game id,id)
  v2-verify    Dry-run verify_game for games (--game id,id) and print why settlement would revert
  v2-beasts    Check the bot's beast derivation and damage against real V2 games, packet by packet (--game id)
  v2-leaderboard Leaderboards of the V2 dungeons from the lootsurvivor.io API (--ids 0-15 minter ids, --levels scores to rank)
  v2-audit     Audit the engine against real V2 games: replay each packet on chain and compare with engine draws (--address owner --game id --draws n)
  frontend     List the dungeons lootsurvivor.io offers now (new ones highlighted); writes data/frontend/dungeons.json
